WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.050
Welcome to Seodaemun-gu!

2
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.350
Sorting your trash correctly isn't hard.

3
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.800
Trash falls into general waste,
food waste, recyclables,

4
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.300
and bulky &amp; special
waste: four types in all.

5
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.350
Here's A, a student who just moved in!

6
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.180
The bag types are confusing,

7
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.700
and A doesn't know if bags from
the old district still work.

8
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.650
<c.note>[On screen] General waste: pay-as-you-throw bag</c>
<c.note>Food waste: food waste bag · Another district's bag ✕</c>

9
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.200
<c.note>[On screen] Pay-as-you-throw bag = the official paid trash bag</c>
<c.note>set by each district (sold at convenience stores and marts)</c>

10
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.220
What if you casually put
trash out in the daytime

11
00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.600
under a street tree or
by a neighbor's door?

12
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.700
Breaking the disposal
rules can get you fined!

13
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.500
Be sure to check the rules
for your neighborhood.

14
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.250
<c.note>[On screen] Fines: not using official bags ₩200,000</c>
<c.note>Wrong time, day or place ₩100,000 · Mixing waste ₩100,000</c>

15
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.350
If your trash wasn't collected,
<c.note>[On screen] ☑ Wrong bag  ☐ Mixed waste  ☐ Wrong time</c>

16
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.850
check the reason on the
“not collected” sticker,

17
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.600
fix it,

18
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.750
and put it out again on
the next collection day.

19
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.600
Don't worry!

20
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.120
Just scan the QR code on your
dorm entrance or collection point

21
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.600
to open the guide.

22
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.000
You can check the exact collection days

23
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.600
for your own neighborhood right away.

24
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.200
<c.note>[On screen] e.g. Yeonhui-dong → Tue, Thu &amp; Sun evenings</c>

25
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.400
Use the QR code to easily look
up how to throw things out.

26
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.700
First: where to put it out!

27
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.450
Houses and shops: in front
of your own home or shop.

28
00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.300
Apartments and dorms: at the
designated spot in your complex.

29
00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:06.600
<c.note>[On screen] Apartments · university dorms:</c>
<c.note>be sure to check with the building manager</c>

30
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.000
Second: when to put it out!

31
00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:13.450
Put it out on your collection
days between 6 and 11 p.m.

32
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.700
Third: the four rules of recycling!

33
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.880
Remember: empty,

34
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.680
Remember: empty, rinse,

35
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.480
Remember: empty, rinse, separate,

36
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.900
Remember: empty, rinse,
separate, and don't mix.

37
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.050
Time for a quick quiz!

38
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:41.500
In Seodaemun-gu, can you use another district's
bags or put trash out in the daytime?

39
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.100
The answer to both is X: no!

40
00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.700
<c.note>[On screen] ✕ Use Seodaemun-gu's own bags</c>
<c.note>✕ Put it out from 6 PM to 11 PM</c>

41
00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.300
Let's keep Seodaemun-gu clean!

42
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.560
If you have trash to throw out today,

43
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.200
check it with the QR code right now!

44
00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.600
<c.note>[On screen] Contact: Seodaemun-gu Office,</c>
<c.note>Sanitation Administration Division · www.sdm.go.kr</c>
